course: dictionary
lesson: 11128
title: Sound words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sound word copies the noise it describes, so you can almost hear it on the page. Whoosh is one of these words. Say it aloud and you can hear something rushing past very fast.
explain: In «The curtain fell whoosh!» the word tells you the curtain dropped quickly, with a rush of air. Whoosh can be a noun (a whoosh of wind), a verb (a slide might whoosh down a hill), or a word on its own, as in «whoosh!»
explain: Sound words also show how something happens, not just what it is. «The smoke came down puff!» and «the milk-pot cracked ffft» both give the reader a sound to hear, so the story feels real. When you meet a sound word, ask: what is making this noise, and how fast or loud is it?
fact: Onomatopoeia means a word that copies the sound it describes.
fact: «Whoosh» means a sound of something moving very fast through the air, or a rush of wind or water.
fact: As a verb, «whoosh» means to move fast with this sound, like a rocket or a train.
fact: As an interjection, «whoosh!» is a word that copies the sound, and it can stand alone.
exercise: «The curtain fell whoosh!» What does whoosh copy? | *A fast rush through the air | A gentle tap on glass | A loud bang like a door shutting | A slow, quiet creak
exercise: In English lessons, whoosh is a good example of which kind of word? | A synonym, a word with the same meaning | An antonym, a word with the opposite meaning | *Onomatopoeia, a word that copies a sound | A proper noun, a name for a place
exercise: «The smoke came down puff!» Find and copy the word that copies a sound. | smoke | *puff | down | came
test: Which word from the story copies the sound of a pot cracking? | whoosh | puff | *ffft | curtain
test: What does «a whoosh of wind» mean? | A loud song sung by the wind | A slow, gentle drip of water | *A quick rush of moving air | A stillness with no sound at all
exam: Why do writers use sound words like whoosh in stories? | To make the words longer | *So the reader can hear how fast or loud something is | To make sentences shorter | To show the story is set in the past
